buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Enerpac Tool Group Corp. manufactures and sells a range of industrial products and solutions in the United States, Germany, Australia, Canada, China, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, France, the United Kingdom, and internationally. The company designs, manufactures, and distributes branded hydraulic and mechanical tools; and provides services and tool rentals to the general industrial, refining and petrochemical, industrial maintenance, repair and operations, machining and manufacturing, power generation, infrastructure, mining and other markets. It also provides branded tools, cylinders, pumps, hydraulic torque wrenches, highly engineered heavy lifting technology solutions, and other tools; and maintenance and manpower services; high-force hydraulic and mechanical tools, including cylinders, pumps, valves, bolt tensioners, specialty tools and other miscellaneous products. It markets its branded tools and services primarily under ENERPAC, HYDRATIGHT, LARZEP, DTA the Smart Move, and SIMPLEX brand names through network of distributors, direct sales to OEMs, and select end users. The company was formerly known as Actuant Corporation and changed its name to Enerpac Tool Group Corp. in January 2020. Enerpac Tool Group Corp. was incorporated in 1910 and is headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul E. Sternlieb | CEO, President & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $311K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue falling 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $57K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Enerpac Tool Group Corp. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.0B market cap on $652M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $120M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.45\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.05434627508273381},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(EPAC) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/EPAC_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_111126122601_1794374761.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794374761.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is New Sales Guidance Altering The Investment Case For Enerpac Tool Group (EPAC)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-epac/enerpac-tool-group/news/is-new-sales-guidance-altering-the-investment-case-for-enerp","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794271507.389,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Is Enerpac Tool Group (EPAC) Undervalued After Earnings, 2027 Guidance And ESOP Filing?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-epac/enerpac-tool-group/news/is-enerpac-tool-group-epac-undervalued-after-earnings-2027-g","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793863897.266,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.949,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Capital International Investors Discloses 5.7% Ownership Stake in Enerpac Tool Group","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/capital-international-investors-discloses-57-ownership-stake-in-e